# Do not run dependency install scripts.
#
# Why: better-sqlite3@13 ships prebuilt binaries, but because it contains a
# binding.gyp, plain `npm ci` / `npm install` still tries `node-gyp rebuild`.
# Without a C++ toolchain that fails, npm silently drops the OPTIONAL package,
# and the app quietly falls back to the JSON file backend even though the
# prebuilt binary would have worked. With scripts disabled the prebuild is
# used directly (verified: `npm ci --ignore-scripts` -> require('better-sqlite3') works).
#
# As a side effect no dependency can run arbitrary code at install time. Nothing
# else in this project's dependency tree needs an install script to build or run
# (Next's SWC/esbuild-style binaries are separate optional packages).
ignore-scripts=true
#
# NOTE: ignore-scripts also disables `pre*`/`post*` hooks of `npm run`, so nothing
# in package.json may rely on them (the token check is chained with `&&` in the
# dev/start scripts themselves; tests/launcherScripts.test.ts enforces this).
